<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France: Petition to ban TV channel gets 500,000 signatures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3792c00d5e82925f1acc0620b357839feeb8833478f830d41270e6a27515ab56</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-petition-to-ban-tv-channel-gets-500-000-signatures/a-79833215--e1663c5e85a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-petition-to-ban-tv-channel-gets-500-000-signatures/a-79833215?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Support for the petition has surged since last month's shooting of a Black man by a reported avid viewer of CNews. Critics say the channel, often compared to Fox News, is a platform for anti-immigrant sentiments.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What might Trump have planned for Iran following the midterm election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:063a0bd531e28131e1c083a0132f95a6acf7a66023ec453369ead64ac86b358a</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-might-trump-have-planned-for-iran-following-the-midterm-election/a-79831816--6124fd56a5c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-might-trump-have-planned-for-iran-following-the-midterm-election/a-79831816?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the US midterms could open a window for diplomacy with Iran, they could also unleash a new military escalation. DW spoke with analysts to identify eight factors that could tip the balance toward war or peace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey officials considering options after CAS order to reinstate Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fb5c71f4b0633a585cf6ba53e0d985951beffd2f94268cd3abb75361bacea12</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451--d3d6cb0a329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's ruling body is deciding how to respond to a decision by the Court of Arbitration for Sport that allows Russia back into international competition. Germany hasn't ruled out pulling out as a tournament host.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>European supermarkets targeted in second reported cyberattack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12a12d5d84194f725791f33c1bbbab055aac8977881e619fb65be4192624b1de</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-supermarkets-targeted-in-second-reported-cyberattack/a-79831139--ffc08d673ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-supermarkets-targeted-in-second-reported-cyberattack/a-79831139?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Supermarkets across Europe have been targeted in cyberattacks once again. Three weeks after a defrosting attack in France, supermarkets in Belgium, Estonia, Ireland, Luxembourg and Sweden reported freezer malfunctions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>LA communities kick out Big Oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c8b945735f859b979e9c9482c07ebd8a1123d8a8a60e607f144419518766feb</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843--72df9d2c6283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of advocacy from residents and legal battles with Big Oil, LA has voted to ban drilling and phase out oil extraction in the city. It's the first city in the country to kick the oil industry out.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's chancellor called for Korean unity. Does Seoul want that?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2d03b9389e439218be0fedeb1291129998cf8d0df28cf0e7224cbc8e00b8d0d</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-chancellor-called-for-korean-unity-does-seoul-want-that/a-79830111--6ea0a91567aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-chancellor-called-for-korean-unity-does-seoul-want-that/a-79830111?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany, like Korea, was once divided by rival political systems and by one of the world's most fortified borders. Chancellor Merz called for a reunified Korea during his recent visit — but the prospect seems faint.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global pedestrian Karl Bushby returns home to UK after 28-year trek</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1a2cf4289cfb1485777000858242420d82e8f6fa4decdc4f09cb9ee91dfcca9</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-pedestrian-karl-bushby-returns-home-to-uk-after-28-year-trek/a-79829564--7ba09cf0439f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-pedestrian-karl-bushby-returns-home-to-uk-after-28-year-trek/a-79829564?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Karl Bushby, a British man who traveled 50,000 km without transport over the past 28 years, has come home. Starting in Chile, he crossed the Americas, Russia and parts of Central Asia and Europe — almost all on foot.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda begins withdrawing troops from Somalia after two decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5190046a255fa3db08ce5f25c3339f3e2acc624f744449b50e4c8c2553c2f34f</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:33:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-begins-withdrawing-troops-from-somalia-after-two-decades/a-79829903--679d18eec17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-begins-withdrawing-troops-from-somalia-after-two-decades/a-79829903?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ugandan troops first deployed to Somalia in 2007 as part of an international military coalition to battle Islamic insurgents. But the mission has faced mounting pressure since a US decision to withdraw funding.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Iliana Yotova won the presidential election in Bulgaria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dc61367190421beb168b5842b57101052ce01b6bc5ea453afb53edf46336306</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-iliana-yotova-won-the-presidential-election-in-bulgaria/a-79829019--beeabc4abe9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-iliana-yotova-won-the-presidential-election-in-bulgaria/a-79829019?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iliana Yotova won the presidential election in Bulgaria, promising to be a "president of peace." But the campaign showed how divided Bulgarians are about the war in Ukraine and drone attacks in the Black Sea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will renewed conflict derail Ethiopia's economic growth?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faeecc683902ddbe622d2a8094be99f2dfaa7219cfacb40d20f6e80222a09017</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060--aec9783cc542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's economy is growing strongly. But renewed fighting in the north of the BRICS member state could deter investment, strain public finances and push up the cost of living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>For US Democrats, climate policy is now about energy bills</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4a7682a0085b50ec86ae3b8eafb1a788841c52f2a1c7d41d8ed4281b58ca314</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T08:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/for-us-democrats-climate-policy-is-now-about-energy-bills/a-79808783--16f8aeaa83fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/for-us-democrats-climate-policy-is-now-about-energy-bills/a-79808783?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate change has all but disappeared from Democrats' campaign pitches, replaced by promises to lower electricity bills. So what would the party really do for climate policy should it win control of Congress?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>US: 9 killed in Florida jet crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff254034dd1e3ff42e821211b22407fd02f1b149889359c704b325a87353bba1</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-9-killed-in-florida-jet-crash/a-79825921--676d24e15b63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-9-killed-in-florida-jet-crash/a-79825921?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Learjet plane crashed near a busy road in a residential neighborhood in Palm Beach County, leaving all nine people on board dead and a large crater on ground.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merz says next German president 'must be a woman' — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:575b26dd6c9217dccbbc57c342055c5d0d943ac4e4c40f0b2ed46a41445c4ca0</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-says-next-german-president-must-be-a-woman-report/live-79825749--f592c9770ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-says-next-german-president-must-be-a-woman-report/live-79825749?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier's second term is due to end in March next year. Meanwhile, Merz has called for 'digital sovereignty' in the era of AI. Follow DW for more</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Gandhi vows to step up pressure on Modi at protest rally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:227ce351272e591c352f8d3978c3ca25af0cb4ab43d13d3ca8bdd97c278ce378</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T06:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-vows-to-step-up-pressure-on-modi-at-protest-rally/live-79825419--5510d05af5f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-gandhi-vows-to-step-up-pressure-on-modi-at-protest-rally/live-79825419?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rahul Gandhi said the removal of election chief Gyanesh Kumar will be the first step to getting the country on the right track. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kimi Antonelli makes history as youngest F1 champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b81873ec147b6c10c17391f2039ebc03ae5d3e477befbf1461390bee48dc4cc</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T05:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kimi-antonelli-makes-history-as-youngest-f1-champion/a-79825130--6d0086c2458b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kimi-antonelli-makes-history-as-youngest-f1-champion/a-79825130?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kimi Antonelli became Formula One's youngest world champion and Italy's first since 1953 when he finished third in Sunday's thrilling and crash-hit Mexico City Grand Prix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea to pour billions into AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e467e65098cb180b4152165b5a29b8f60de6dc918486121ddd3b02a70c7d050e</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T05:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-to-pour-billions-into-ai/a-79825118--18a63506a9e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-to-pour-billions-into-ai/a-79825118?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Lee Jae Myung has presented his record-breaking budget proposal for 2027, including major investments in AI and other tech.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia report hacking attacks on emergency alert apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9da686321f945716172d2e2c5c0697aa9110cf99135ff13b27e60bd92d2e45e</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T02:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-report-hacking-attacks-on-emergency-alert-apps/live-79825079--4c88f484410d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-report-hacking-attacks-on-emergency-alert-apps/live-79825079?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Russia have both reported cyberattacks targeting applications used to send emergency alerts to the public. Meanwhile, Zelenskyy said Ukraine will stop refinery strikes if the US sends Patriot missiles.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police investigating after needles found in Halloween candy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:143c294ffbe22e309b5dfb63c530a2f7fda677ef3509b4a8e416d516dddb51b8</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T01:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-investigating-after-needles-found-in-halloween-candy/a-79825051--00c6413d6c8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-investigating-after-needles-found-in-halloween-candy/a-79825051?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German police said they received phone calls with reports about sharp objects concealed in Halloween candy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's giant new radar in Kaliningrad raises alarm in NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8716a00f0746dcdfd0effcb6c676a6bbe41c75e3d282d6a26ce0e65d7f5d9cc5</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815--4cdeadba9801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is nearing completion of what experts think is a giant radar complex in Kaliningrad, capable of monitoring much of Europe. Experts warn the project could intensify the military standoff between Moscow and NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Police chief arrested for abuse of office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d0caf57f639ad8767cc35604e9a6d3ed3322c471798895302c5081ba1f19686</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:34:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-police-chief-arrested-for-abuse-of-office/a-79823382--1db3f61a57a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-police-chief-arrested-for-abuse-of-office/a-79823382?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marko Kricak, an Aleksandar Vucic loyalist, is accused of suppressing and manipulating an investigation into a gangland murder. Prosecutors say the arrest is not linked to Vucic's recent election defeat.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France opens attempted murder probe after protest attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ab0f42d7bdff41ebfee8fb6b5c94c1ba1b2a2412de738cc8380942647ce0172</id><updated>2026-11-02T18:32:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-opens-attempted-murder-probe-after-protest-attack/a-79822853--daa7efa660e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-opens-attempted-murder-probe-after-protest-attack/a-79822853?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paris prosecutors have opened an attempted murder investigation after a Molotov attack on police. France reported 779 arrests during nationwide protests and Halloween night, fewer than on previous weekends.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
